# Actual built-in imagegen prompt

Goal candidate: 4965395d-e0c5-5e23-a408-a11712aab409

Use case: scientific-educational. Create a friendly German chemistry/civic-science learning illustration, hand-drawn comic style, landscape approximately 1600 x 900, opaque light warm background, strong navy outlines and calm pastel colours. Topic: evaluate historical and current societal effects of medicines, using antibiotics as an example. Make a clean readable composition with three large connected visual ideas, no dense paragraphs. LEFT: small warm sepia historical vignette of a mid-20th-century hospital bedside, a doctor handing a generic plain medicine bottle to a recovering seated adult patient; label "Früher". CENTRE: contemporary community pharmacy counter with two different ordinary people seeking access, a generic medicine box and a few simple coins; label "Zugang". RIGHT: a LARGE balanced decision scale: left pan contains a heart with a shield, clearly labelled "Nutzen"; right pan contains stylized bacterial shapes plus a small orange alert icon, clearly labelled "Risiken". A small short subtitle under this pan: "z. B. Resistenzen". This represents an example-specific risk of antibiotic use, not resistance caused by every medication. Above the whole image a short title "Wirkung und Folgen abwägen". A plain open evidence/document icon sits BELOW and OUTSIDE the scale as an input to the decision, never as the benefit on a scale pan. Portray the social evaluation with dignity and no stigma, without brand names, drug doses, treatment recommendations, patient data, grades, claims of guaranteed cure or completely safe medicine. Strong large main motifs and sparse labels readable at 360-pixel overall width. Not photorealistic or a sterile technical infographic.
